# C1-S01 / C1-S01B — Village Gate and the Road Ledger.
# Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 1502–1570.
# Scene: Oakhaven (village / region). No prophecy, no hero's welcome.
# The ledger links Kaelen's personal goal to Oakhaven's problems: he needs the
# south road, and the south road needs fixing.

~ start
Bran: Three hours, Elara. You said one. I had one written down, in ink, and now I'll have to cross it out, and you know what crossings-out do to a ledger.
Elara: I found a problem. It walked most of the way here by itself.
Kaelen: Hi. That's— I'm the problem. Kaelen. Sorry about your three hours.
Bran: Does it talk? Usually they don't talk.
Elara: You'll wish it didn't. It apologises to everything, me included.
Kaelen: I'm right here. And to be fair to me, you've only seen me on a bad day.
Bran: ...Hold still. That grey on your boots is crater dust; spit won't shift it. You came down from the north, lad.
Elara: From the crater, Bran.
Bran: Elara.
Elara: I know. Don't write it down yet.
Bran: Does Mara know yet? I'd like it on record that I asked, before she tells everyone I didn't.
Elara: Why would Mara know? Nobody's seen him but you.
Bran: Mara knows everything by lunch.
Mara: I heard that! Has it eaten? Is it staying? Why's it still standing in your gate when my oven's hot?
Bran: See? Not even lunch yet. That's going in the ledger, and I'm underlining "not even".
set ch1_oakhaven_entered
do gate_opens

~ ledger
Kaelen: Elara said you keep road records. Travellers, strangers, things that fall out of places.
Bran: I keep the arguments written down, so everyone can have exactly the same argument again next spring. It's called civic memory. Nobody thanks me for it.
Kaelen: Has anyone else come out of the crater? Before me? There were a lot of us on that plane.
Bran: What, today? Today it's just you, and I've not even found a column for you yet.
Kaelen: Any day. Ever. I'll take anything with a date next to it.
do bran_opens_ledger
# Mostly caravans, weather closures, missing goats, patrol notes. A few old
# entries are marked NORTHFALL.
Bran: We've found people up north before. Near the crater, mind, not in it. One at a time, usually.
Kaelen: "Usually." How usual is usually? A number, please. Any number.
Bran: No number, lad. Rare enough that we remember them, common enough that I stopped saying "impossible". The ledger calls them Northfalls.
do ledger_entry_highlight
Kaelen: This one says "transferred to Ironhold Arrival Registry". Transferred. Somebody went somewhere.
Bran: Years back, that one. Name's gone, the ink ran. Ironhold took them, whoever they were.
# This entry is Seraphina. Nobody, the player included, can know that yet.
set ch1_northfall_registry_seen
Kaelen: Then that's where I'm going. Ironhold, and their registry, and whatever names are in it.
Bran: Then you need the south road. And the south road's no good without the old watch route, and the old watch route—
Elara: —which has been bad all week.
Bran: Thank you, Elara. And the north field's worse than the watch route, which I'd have said myself if I'd been let finish.
Kaelen: How much worse? Give me them in order. I'll take them one at a time.
Bran: You've turned up on a very educational day, lad. I'm starting you a page. Don't make me cross it out.
do journal Lead: the Ironhold Arrival Registry. Blocker: Oakhaven's road south is unsafe.
